<title>ITALY: Details of Italian budget.</title>
<headline>Details of Italian budget.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the Italian government's 1997 budget. Some items have yet to be fully defined. (all figures in billions of lire):</p>
<p>Savings in state spending:</p>
<p>* Health Spending:</p>
<p>    - Hospital rationalisation				560</p>
<p>    - Savings in drug costs				   640</p>
<p>* Public Administration:</p>
<p>    - Defence cuts						780</p>
<p>    - Some full-time jobs turned into part-time work  620</p>
<p>    - Rationalisation within schools			500</p>
<p>    - Hiring freeze in some sectors			 100</p>
<p>    - 10 pct cut in overtime spending		     100</p>
<p>    - Other measures					    300</p>
<p>* Local Spending:</p>
<p>    - Reduction in transfers to local councils	4,660</p>
<p>* Pension and Welfare Spending:</p>
<p>    - Crackdown on pension fraud and recovery of</p>
<p>	some contributions				    2,782</p>
<p>    - Harmonisation of pensions contributions	 2,375</p>
<p>- Delay in &quot;liquidation&quot; cash handout to people</p>
<p>	retiring from the state sector			810</p>
<p>    - Crackdown against invalidity pension fraud	130</p>
<p>* Public Services:</p>
<p>    - Savings at state railways (FS)			640</p>
<p>    - Savings in postal service			     550</p>
<p>    - Lay-off schemes at post, FS, and Monopoli group 150</p>
<p>    - Rationalisation of handouts to public bank</p>
<p>	Mediocredit and export credit agency SACE     1,000</p>
<p>* Various:</p>
<p>    - Reduction in money for public service offices    90</p>
<p>    - Reduction in forward payments</p>
<p>	   on public contracts				  700</p>
<p>    - Reduction in number of official state cars	 15</p>
<p>    - Other measures					    195</p>
<p>=====================================================</p>
<p>    Total							17,700</p>
<p>Other savings</p>
<p>     - Reduction of funds to the ministries	   1,500</p>
<p>     - Measures to reduce various budget demands    2,500</p>
<p>     - Re-structuring of transfers to FS		3,000</p>
<p>     - Acceleration of bureaucracy to free up</p>
<p>	 European Union financing			   1,000</p>
<p>=====================================================</p>
<p>    Total							 8,000</p>
<p>Fresh Revenues</p>
<p>    - Crack down on fiscal fraud			  3,309</p>
<p>    - Taxing fringe-benefits (including company</p>
<p>	cars and luncheon vouchers)			 2,555</p>
<p>    - State lotteries and other games		   1,000</p>
<p>    - Other unspecified items			     1,351</p>
<p>    - Other measures to be unveiled before the end</p>
<p>	 of the year. (widely reported in the press to</p>
<p>	 include value added tax hikes and increased</p>
<p>	 duty on unleaded petrol)			   4,285</p>
<p>=====================================================</p>
<p>    Total							12,500</p>
<p>Additional measures</p>
<p>    - &quot;Europe Tax&quot; (to be detailed before year end)13,000</p>
<p>    - Unspecified &quot;Treasury operations&quot;		12,000</p>
<p>=====================================================</p>
<p>    Total							25,000</p>
<p>-- Rome newsroom +396 6782501</p>
</text>
